 and the ability to generate primary cilia. <source>Nat. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>7</volume>:<fpage>517</fpage>&#x02013;524.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15852003</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal">Lutcke, A., S. Jansson, R.G. Parton, P. Chavrier, A. Valencia, L.A. Huber, E. Lehtonen, and M. Zerial. <year>1993</year>. Rab17, a novel small GTPase, is specific for epithelial cells and is induced during cell polarization. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>121</volume>:<fpage>553</fpage>&#x02013;564.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8486736</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal">Michaud, E.J., and B.K. Yoder. <year>2006</year>. The primary cilium in cell signaling and cancer. <source>Cancer Res.</source> <volume>66</volume>:<fpage>6463</fpage>&#x02013;6467.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16818613</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal">Pfeffer, S. <year>2003</year>. Membrane domains in the secretory and endocytic pathways. <source>Cell.</source> <volume>112</volume>:<fpage>507</fpage>&#x02013;517.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12600314</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal">Qin, H., Z. Wang, D. Diener, and J. Rosenbaum. <year>2007</year>. Intraflagellar transport protein 27 is a small G protein involved in cell-cycle control. <source>Curr. Biol.</source> <volume>17</volume>:<fpage>193</fpage>&#x02013;202.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17276912</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal">Sahlender, D.A., R.C. Roberts, S.D. Arden, G. Spudich, M.J. Taylor, J.P. Luzio, J. Kendrick-Jones, and F. Buss. <year>2005</year>. Optineurin links myosin VI to the Golgi complex and is involved in Golgi organization and exocytosis. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>169</volume>:<fpage>285</fpage>&#x02013;295.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15837803</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><citation citation-type="journal">Schafer, J.C., M.E. Winkelbauer, C.L. Williams, C.J. Haycraft, R.A. Desmond, and B.K. Yoder. <year>2006</year>. IFTA-2 is a conserved cilia protein involved in pathways regulating longevity and dauer formation in <italic>Caenorhabditis elegans.</italic> <source>J. Cell Sci.</source> <volume>119</volume>:<fpage>4088</fpage>&#x02013;4100.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16968739</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib26"><citation citation-type="journal">Scholey, J.M. <year>2003</year>. Intraflagellar transport. <source>Annu. Rev. Cell Dev. Biol.</source> <volume>19</volume>:<fpage>423</fpage>&#x02013;443.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14570576</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib27"><citation citation-type="journal">Shorter, J., R. Watson, M.E. Giannakou, M. Clarke, G. Warren, and F.A. Barr. <year>1999</year>. GRASP55, a second mammalian GRASP protein involved in the stacking of Golgi cisternae in a cell-free system. <source>EMBO J.</source> <volume>18</volume>:<fpage>4949</fpage>&#x02013;4960.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10487747</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib28"><citation citation-type="journal">Singla, V., and J.F. Reiter. <year>2006</year>. The primary cilium as the cell's antenna: signaling at a sensory organelle. <source>Science.</source> <volume>313</volume>:<fpage>629</fpage>&#x02013;633.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16888132</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib29"><citation citation-type="journal">Sorokin, S.P. <year>1968</year>. Reconstructions of centriole formation and ciliogenesis in mammalian lungs. <source>J. Cell Sci.</source> <volume>3</volume>:<fpage>207</fpage>&#x02013;230.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">5661997</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib30"><citation citation-type="journal">Zacchi, P., H. Stenmark, R.G. Parton, D. Orioli, F. Lim, A. Giner, I. Mellman, M. Zerial, and C. Murphy. <year>1998</year>. Rab17 regulates membrane trafficking through apical recycling endosomes in polarized epithelial cells. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>140</volume>:<fpage>1039</fpage>&#x02013;1053.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9490718</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib31"><citation citation-type="journal">Zerial, M., and H. McBride. <year>2001</year>. Rab proteins as membrane organizers. <source>Nat. Rev. Mol. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>2</volume>:<fpage>107</fpage>&#x02013;117.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11252952</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib32"><citation citation-type="journal">Zhou, C., L. Cunningham, A.I. Marcus, Y. Li, and R.A. Kahn. <year>2006</year>. Arl2 and Arl3 regulate different microtubule-dependent processes. <source>Mol. Biol. Cell.</source> <volume>17</volume>:<fpage>2476</fpage>&#x02013;2487.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16525022</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>